  "body": "### What is the expected enhancement?\r\n\r\nCurrently, VQC only accepts one-hot encoded input. It might be beneficial to accept categorical labels (and perhaps features) to limit friction for new adopters used to scikit-learn—ideally, they could just replace their classical code with the quantum equivalent without explicitly performing the encoding themselves. The only downside is this does contribute to code bloat.\r\n\r\nThis was raised previously in #62 for VQC and NeuralNetworkClassifier. It looks like this capacity was incorporated into the parent class in #143, but, as far as I can tell, VQC is still limited to one-hot encoding.\r\n\r\nThere might be a good reason for this, but, if not, we should ensure that VQC inherits this behaviour properly.",
